IMPORT `P2-section-2-gate`

-- P2-art-10: Article 10 (data and data governance) of the EU Artificial Intelligence Act, Regulation (EU) 2024/1689 as amended by Regulation (EU) 2026/1744.
-- The Omnibus replaced paragraphs 1 and 6 (the cross-references to paragraph 5 became cross-references to Article 4a(1)) and deleted paragraph 5 (its text, as enacted, is in P2-art-4a.l4, next to Article 4a).
-- Paragraphs 1 and 6 are encoded in both versions: each text in its own function with no date and no gate, and a dispatcher gated by Article 113 (with Article 111(2)) that reads the version in force on the date asked.
-- The branch of a dispatcher that reads the text as enacted is dead: Chapter III Sections 1 to 3 applied as enacted from 2 August 2026, after the Omnibus took effect (27 July 2026). The old text is tested through its own function.
-- Reading a result: JUST TRUE the requirement is met on the facts; JUST FALSE the text says no; NOTHING not covered.

§ `Article 10(1): data sets that meet the quality criteria`

-- src:eu-ai-act-2024-1689:745 | 1. High-risk AI systems which make use of techniques involving the training of AI models with data shall be developed on the basis of training, validation and testing data sets that meet the quality criteria referred to in paragraphs 2 to 5 whenever such data sets are used.
@ref Art 10(1) as enacted (src:eu-ai-act-2024-1689:745)
-- VERSION as enacted: the quality criteria are those of paragraphs 2 to 5 (here paragraphs 2, 3 and 4, and paragraph 5, the special-categories paragraph).
-- No date and no gate: the dispatcher below applies Article 113 and reads the version.
GIVEN `the high-risk AI system makes use of techniques involving the training of AI models with data` IS A BOOLEAN
      `training, validation and testing data sets are used` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the data sets used meet the quality criteria referred to in paragraphs 2, 3 and 4 of this Article` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the data sets used meet the quality criteria referred to in paragraph 5 of this Article` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 10(1) as enacted the high-risk AI system is developed on the basis of data sets that meet the quality criteria` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the high-risk AI system makes use of techniques involving the training of AI models with data`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "High-risk AI systems which make use of techniques involving the training of AI models with data"
    ELSE IF NOT (`training, validation and testing data sets are used`)
         THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "whenever such data sets are used": a duty whose "whenever" is unmet, fork F-duty-where
         ELSE JUST (`the data sets used meet the quality criteria referred to in paragraphs 2, 3 and 4 of this Article` AND `the data sets used meet the quality criteria referred to in paragraph 5 of this Article`)  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall be developed on the basis of training, validation and testing data sets that meet the quality criteria referred to in paragraphs 2 to 5 whenever such data sets are used"

-- src:292 | 1. High-risk AI systems which make use of techniques involving the training of AI models with data shall be developed on the basis of training, validation and testing data sets that meet the quality criteria referred to in paragraphs 2, 3 and 4 of this Article and in Article 4a(1) whenever such data sets are used.
@ref Art 10(1) as amended (src:292)
-- VERSION as amended: paragraph 5 is deleted; the criteria are those of paragraphs 2, 3 and 4 and of Article 4a(1) (seam: the answer of Article 4a(1) is a plain input here).
GIVEN `the high-risk AI system makes use of techniques involving the training of AI models with data` IS A BOOLEAN
      `training, validation and testing data sets are used` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the data sets used meet the quality criteria referred to in paragraphs 2, 3 and 4 of this Article` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the data sets used meet the quality criteria referred to in Article 4a(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 10(1) as amended the high-risk AI system is developed on the basis of data sets that meet the quality criteria` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the high-risk AI system makes use of techniques involving the training of AI models with data`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "High-risk AI systems which make use of techniques involving the training of AI models with data"
    ELSE IF NOT (`training, validation and testing data sets are used`)
         THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "whenever such data sets are used": a duty whose "whenever" is unmet, fork F-duty-where
         ELSE JUST (`the data sets used meet the quality criteria referred to in paragraphs 2, 3 and 4 of this Article` AND `the data sets used meet the quality criteria referred to in Article 4a(1)`)  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall be developed on the basis of training, validation and testing data sets that meet the quality criteria referred to in paragraphs 2, 3 and 4 of this Article and in Article 4a(1) whenever such data sets are used"

-- src:292 | 1. High-risk AI systems which make use of techniques involving the training of AI models with data shall be developed on the basis of training, validation and testing data sets that meet the quality criteria referred to in paragraphs 2, 3 and 4 of this Article and in Article 4a(1) whenever such data sets are used.
-- src:eu-ai-act-2024-1689:745 | 1. High-risk AI systems which make use of techniques involving the training of AI models with data shall be developed on the basis of training, validation and testing data sets that meet the quality criteria referred to in paragraphs 2 to 5 whenever such data sets are used.
@ref Art 10(1) (src:292) (src:eu-ai-act-2024-1689:745)
-- Dispatcher: gated by Article 113 (Chapter III Sections 1 to 3) and Article 111(2), then it reads the version in force on the date asked.
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system` IS AN `AI system`
      `the harmonisation facts` IS A `Arts 8 to 15 harmonisation facts`
      `the high-risk AI system makes use of techniques involving the training of AI models with data` IS A BOOLEAN
      `training, validation and testing data sets are used` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the data sets used meet the quality criteria referred to in paragraphs 2, 3 and 4 of this Article` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the data sets used meet the quality criteria referred to in paragraph 5 of this Article` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the data sets used meet the quality criteria referred to in Article 4a(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 10(1) the high-risk AI system is developed on the basis of data sets that meet the quality criteria` MEANS
    CONSIDER `Arts 8 to 15 the gate for the requirement` `the date asked` `the AI system` `the harmonisation facts` (`Article reference` OF 10, "", 1)
    WHEN `Arts 8 to 15 gate the requirement applies` THEN
        CONSIDER `Omnibus Art 4 the version in force` `the date asked`
        WHEN `as enacted` THEN `Art 10(1) as enacted the high-risk AI system is developed on the basis of data sets that meet the quality criteria` `the high-risk AI system makes use of techniques involving the training of AI models with data` `training, validation and testing data sets are used` `the data sets used meet the quality criteria referred to in paragraphs 2, 3 and 4 of this Article` `the data sets used meet the quality criteria referred to in paragraph 5 of this Article`  -- VERSION as enacted
        WHEN `as amended` THEN `Art 10(1) as amended the high-risk AI system is developed on the basis of data sets that meet the quality criteria` `the high-risk AI system makes use of techniques involving the training of AI models with data` `training, validation and testing data sets are used` `the data sets used meet the quality criteria referred to in paragraphs 2, 3 and 4 of this Article` `the data sets used meet the quality criteria referred to in Article 4a(1)`  -- VERSION as amended
    WHEN `Arts 8 to 15 gate cut off by Article 2(2)` THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): Article 2(2) "only Article 6(1), Article 60a and Articles 102 to 112 shall apply" to a high-risk AI system under Article 6(1) related to Section B products (seam S14, the keel's answer)
    WHEN `Arts 8 to 15 gate may be limited under Article 2(13)` THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): Article 2(13) says the application of this requirement "may be limited"; how far is for the delegated acts it names
    OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapter III Section 2 applies from the date Article 113(c) gives, and Article 111(2) saves a system placed earlier and not significantly changed


§ `Article 10(2): data governance and management practices`

-- src:294 | 2. Training, validation and testing data sets shall be subject to data governance and management practices appropriate for the intended purpose of the high-risk AI system. Those practices shall concern in particular:
-- src:295 | (a) the relevant design choices;
-- src:296 | (b) data collection processes and the origin of data, and in the case of personal data, the original purpose of the data collection;
-- src:297 | (c) relevant data-preparation processing operations, such as annotation, labelling, cleaning, updating, enrichment and aggregation;
-- src:298 | (d) the formulation of assumptions, in particular with respect to the information that the data are supposed to measure and represent;
-- src:299 | (e) an assessment of the availability, quantity and suitability of the data sets that are needed;
-- src:300 | (f) examination in view of possible biases that are likely to affect the health and safety of persons, have a negative impact on fundamental rights or lead to discrimination prohibited under Union law, especially where data outputs influence inputs for future operations;
-- src:301 | (g) appropriate measures to detect, prevent and mitigate possible biases identified according to point (f);
-- src:302 | (h) the identification of relevant data gaps or shortcomings that prevent compliance with this Regulation, and how those gaps and shortcomings can be addressed.
@ref Art 10(2) (src:294-302)
-- "in particular": the list gives the matters the practices shall concern at least; each listed matter is needed (a matter not concerned is the text's no).
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system` IS AN `AI system`
      `the harmonisation facts` IS A `Arts 8 to 15 harmonisation facts`
      `the training, validation and testing data sets are subject to data governance and management practices appropriate for the intended purpose of the high-risk AI system` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the practices concern the relevant design choices` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the practices concern data collection processes and the origin of data, and in the case of personal data, the original purpose of the data collection` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the practices concern relevant data-preparation processing operations, such as annotation, labelling, cleaning, updating, enrichment and aggregation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the practices concern the formulation of assumptions, in particular with respect to the information that the data are supposed to measure and represent` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the practices concern an assessment of the availability, quantity and suitability of the data sets that are needed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the practices concern examination in view of possible biases that are likely to affect the health and safety of persons, have a negative impact on fundamental rights or lead to discrimination prohibited under Union law, especially where data outputs influence inputs for future operations` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the practices concern appropriate measures to detect, prevent and mitigate possible biases identified according to point (f)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the practices concern the identification of relevant data gaps or shortcomings that prevent compliance with this Regulation, and how those gaps and shortcomings can be addressed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 10(2) the data sets are subject to data governance and management practices appropriate for the intended purpose, which concern the following` MEANS
    CONSIDER `Arts 8 to 15 the gate for the requirement` `the date asked` `the AI system` `the harmonisation facts` (`Article reference` OF 10, "", 2)
    WHEN `Arts 8 to 15 gate the requirement applies` THEN
        JUST (`the training, validation and testing data sets are subject to data governance and management practices appropriate for the intended purpose of the high-risk AI system` AND `the practices concern the relevant design choices` AND `the practices concern data collection processes and the origin of data, and in the case of personal data, the original purpose of the data collection` AND `the practices concern relevant data-preparation processing operations, such as annotation, labelling, cleaning, updating, enrichment and aggregation` AND `the practices concern the formulation of assumptions, in particular with respect to the information that the data are supposed to measure and represent` AND `the practices concern an assessment of the availability, quantity and suitability of the data sets that are needed` AND `the practices concern examination in view of possible biases that are likely to affect the health and safety of persons, have a negative impact on fundamental rights or lead to discrimination prohibited under Union law, especially where data outputs influence inputs for future operations` AND `the practices concern appropriate measures to detect, prevent and mitigate possible biases identified according to point (f)` AND `the practices concern the identification of relevant data gaps or shortcomings that prevent compliance with this Regulation, and how those gaps and shortcomings can be addressed`)  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Training, validation and testing data sets shall be subject to data governance and management practices appropriate for the intended purpose ... Those practices shall concern in particular"
    WHEN `Arts 8 to 15 gate cut off by Article 2(2)` THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): Article 2(2) "only Article 6(1), Article 60a and Articles 102 to 112 shall apply" to a high-risk AI system under Article 6(1) related to Section B products (seam S14, the keel's answer)
    WHEN `Arts 8 to 15 gate may be limited under Article 2(13)` THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): Article 2(13) says the application of this requirement "may be limited"; how far is for the delegated acts it names
    OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapter III Section 2 applies from the date Article 113(c) gives, and Article 111(2) saves a system placed earlier and not significantly changed


§ `Article 10(3): the quality of the data sets`

-- src:303 | Training, validation and testing data sets shall be relevant, sufficiently representative, and to the best extent possible, free of errors and complete in view of the intended purpose.
@ref Art 10(3) first sentence (src:303)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system` IS AN `AI system`
      `the harmonisation facts` IS A `Arts 8 to 15 harmonisation facts`
      `the training, validation and testing data sets are relevant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the data sets are sufficiently representative` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the data sets are, to the best extent possible, free of errors and complete in view of the intended purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 10(3) first sentence the data sets are relevant, sufficiently representative, and to the best extent possible, free of errors and complete` MEANS
    CONSIDER `Arts 8 to 15 the gate for the requirement` `the date asked` `the AI system` `the harmonisation facts` (`Article reference` OF 10, "", 3)
    WHEN `Arts 8 to 15 gate the requirement applies` THEN
        JUST (`the training, validation and testing data sets are relevant` AND `the data sets are sufficiently representative` AND `the data sets are, to the best extent possible, free of errors and complete in view of the intended purpose`)  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Training, validation and testing data sets shall be relevant, sufficiently representative, and to the best extent possible, free of errors and complete in view of the intended purpose"
    WHEN `Arts 8 to 15 gate cut off by Article 2(2)` THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): Article 2(2) "only Article 6(1), Article 60a and Articles 102 to 112 shall apply" to a high-risk AI system under Article 6(1) related to Section B products (seam S14, the keel's answer)
    WHEN `Arts 8 to 15 gate may be limited under Article 2(13)` THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): Article 2(13) says the application of this requirement "may be limited"; how far is for the delegated acts it names
    OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapter III Section 2 applies from the date Article 113(c) gives, and Article 111(2) saves a system placed earlier and not significantly changed

-- src:303 | They shall have the appropriate statistical properties, including, where applicable, as regards the persons or groups of persons in relation to whom the high-risk AI system is intended to be used.
@ref Art 10(3) second sentence (src:303)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system` IS AN `AI system`
      `the harmonisation facts` IS A `Arts 8 to 15 harmonisation facts`
      `the data sets have the appropriate statistical properties` IS A BOOLEAN
      `where applicable, the data sets have the appropriate statistical properties as regards the persons or groups of persons in relation to whom the high-risk AI system is intended to be used` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 10(3) second sentence the data sets have the appropriate statistical properties` MEANS
    CONSIDER `Arts 8 to 15 the gate for the requirement` `the date asked` `the AI system` `the harmonisation facts` (`Article reference` OF 10, "", 3)
    WHEN `Arts 8 to 15 gate the requirement applies` THEN
        JUST (`the data sets have the appropriate statistical properties` AND `where applicable, the data sets have the appropriate statistical properties as regards the persons or groups of persons in relation to whom the high-risk AI system is intended to be used`)  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "They shall have the appropriate statistical properties, including, where applicable, as regards the persons or groups of persons in relation to whom the high-risk AI system is intended to be used"
    WHEN `Arts 8 to 15 gate cut off by Article 2(2)` THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): Article 2(2) "only Article 6(1), Article 60a and Articles 102 to 112 shall apply" to a high-risk AI system under Article 6(1) related to Section B products (seam S14, the keel's answer)
    WHEN `Arts 8 to 15 gate may be limited under Article 2(13)` THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): Article 2(13) says the application of this requirement "may be limited"; how far is for the delegated acts it names
    OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapter III Section 2 applies from the date Article 113(c) gives, and Article 111(2) saves a system placed earlier and not significantly changed

-- src:303 | Those characteristics of the data sets may be met at the level of individual data sets or at the level of a combination thereof.
@ref Art 10(3) third sentence (src:303)
-- A liberty ("may be met").
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system` IS AN `AI system`
      `the harmonisation facts` IS A `Arts 8 to 15 harmonisation facts`
      `the characteristics are met at the level of individual data sets or at the level of a combination thereof` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 10(3) third sentence the characteristics of the data sets may be met at the level of individual data sets or of a combination thereof` MEANS
    CONSIDER `Arts 8 to 15 the gate for the requirement` `the date asked` `the AI system` `the harmonisation facts` (`Article reference` OF 10, "", 3)
    WHEN `Arts 8 to 15 gate the requirement applies` THEN
        IF NOT (`the characteristics are met at the level of individual data sets or at the level of a combination thereof`)
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): "may be met at the level of individual data sets or at the level of a combination thereof": the sentence permits two levels and says nothing of any other
        ELSE JUST (TRUE)
    WHEN `Arts 8 to 15 gate cut off by Article 2(2)` THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): Article 2(2) "only Article 6(1), Article 60a and Articles 102 to 112 shall apply" to a high-risk AI system under Article 6(1) related to Section B products (seam S14, the keel's answer)
    WHEN `Arts 8 to 15 gate may be limited under Article 2(13)` THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): Article 2(13) says the application of this requirement "may be limited"; how far is for the delegated acts it names
    OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapter III Section 2 applies from the date Article 113(c) gives, and Article 111(2) saves a system placed earlier and not significantly changed


