§ `Article 10(6): development without training techniques`

-- src:eu-ai-act-2024-1689:778 | 6. For the development of high-risk AI systems not using techniques involving the training of AI models, paragraphs 2 to 5 apply only to the testing data sets.
@ref Art 10(6) as enacted (src:eu-ai-act-2024-1689:778)
-- VERSION as enacted. The question is about one paragraph at a time: the paragraph of Article 10 (a number), or Article 4a(1).
GIVEN `the high-risk AI system is developed not using techniques involving the training of AI models` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the paragraph of Article 10 the question is about, as a number (0 if none)` IS A NUMBER
      `the question is about Article 4a(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the data set is a testing data set` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 10(6) as enacted the paragraph applies to the data set` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the high-risk AI system is developed not using techniques involving the training of AI models`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "For the development of high-risk AI systems not using techniques involving the training of AI models"
    ELSE IF NOT (`the paragraph of Article 10 the question is about, as a number (0 if none)` AT LEAST 2 AND `the paragraph of Article 10 the question is about, as a number (0 if none)` AT MOST 5)
         THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "paragraphs 2 to 5": the paragraphs the sentence names (as enacted; Article 4a(1) is not in that text)
         ELSE JUST (`the data set is a testing data set`)  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "paragraphs 2 to 5 apply only to the testing data sets"

